en|Little is known about him. He was the son of Cornelis Pietersz van Soest,
en|and in 1642 he became Poorter of Amsterdam where he was recorded until 1667.
en|In April 1643, as a painter living on the Nieuwezijds Voorburgwal, 
en|he married Marritie Dircx (born ca. 1620 in Goch).
en|Jan Abrahamsz Beerstraaten was one of his pupils.
en|Among his subjects are the Battle of the Downs and the Second Anglo-Dutch War, 
en|particularly the Raid on the Medway. Van Soest also depicted the ships 
en|Comet Star and Eendracht. His paintings usually have a panoramic view of the battles. 
en|Van Soest rendered ships with delicate brushstrokes, while a light impasto is a feature of his skies.
en|The Unified Socialist League was led by Kasuga Shōjirō, formerly a leading figure in the Japanese Communist Party. 
en|Makoto Omori was the general secretary of the organization. 
en|The organization emerged from a split from the Preparatory Communission for a 
en|Socialist Reform Movement (a.k.a. the 'Socialist Renovation' group). 
en|The membership of the Unified Socialist League (numbering around 600) 
en|was dominated by students, and the organization had a student wing called the Socialist Student Front.
en|The Unified Socialist League repeatedly attacked the Communist Party of Japan,
en|arguing that the party lacked internal democracy and that it was subservient to Chinese interests.
en|The Unified Socialist League did not put forth candidates in national elections.
en|Thetford Academy is a coeducational independent school in Thetford, Vermont. 
en|Located at 304 Academy Road in Thetford Center, Vermont, it is the state's oldest secondary school.
en|Thetford Academy celebrated its bicentennial year in 2018–2019.
en|It is a tax-exempt non-profit institution under section 501(c)(3).
en|A historic New England Town Academy (one of approximately 20 remaining in Vermont, New Hampshire, Maine, and Connecticut),
en|Thetford Academy serves as the designated public school for the town of Thetford. 
en|The academy also has partnership agreements with the town of Lyme, New Hampshire,
en|and serves several towns that provide students a choice of high schools, 
en|or do not have a high school of their own. Thetford Academy also hosts a small 
en|contingent of international students from countries including China, South Korea, 
en|Greece, and Rwanda. In the 2022–2023 school year, Thetford Academy had 312 students enrolled in grades 7–12.
en|Thetford Academy offers programs in Arts, Humanities, STEM, and Wellness.
en|Its Unified Arts curriculum includes programs in visual arts, design technology, drama, music, and culinary arts.
en|Its Humanities program includes courses in English, social studies, and world languages.
en|Thetford Academy's STEM curriculum focuses on science, technology, engineering, and mathematics.
en|The academy's Wellness program contains courses in physical education and health.
en|Some programs are aimed at grades seven and eight, some at grades ten to twelve, 
en|some grades eleven and twelve, and some grades nine to twelve.
en|Haddock began as a street performer, but he later focused his creative energies into screenwriting for television.
en|One of his earliest efforts in writing was for the popular series, MacGyver, where he also served 
en|as the story editor and executive story editor.
en|He founded his production company Haddock Entertainment in 1997,
en|and is best known for his Vancouver-based television drama creations Da Vinci's Inquest (1998–2005),
en|Da Vinci's City Hall (2005–2006), Intelligence (2006–2007), and The Romeo Section (2015–2016), 
en|which frequently feature notable locations around the city.
en|He also served as writer/co-executive producer on the Martin Scorsese HBO production Boardwalk Empire, 
en|and was nominated for a Writers Guild of America award for that show.
en|Haddock's stage play Helen Lawrence was staged internationally in 2014, including stints at the prestigious Edinburgh International Festival, 
en|Toronto's Canadian Stage, Munich and Vancouver.
en|New Wave Salsa is the fourth studio album recorded by Puerto Rican singer Eddie Santiago
en|Bullionism is an economic theory that defines wealth by the amount of precious metals owned.
en|[1] Bullionism is an early and perhaps more primitive form of mercantilism.[citation needed] 
en|It was derived, during the 16th century, from the observation that the Kingdom of England, 
en|because of its large trade surplus, possessed large amounts of gold and silver—bullion—despite 
en|the fact that there was not any mining of precious metals in England.
en|Thomas Milles (1550–1627) and others recommended that England increase exports
en|to create a trade surplus, convert the surplus into precious metals,
en|and hinder the drain of money and precious metal to other countries. 
en|England did restrict exportation of money or precious metals around 1600, 
en|but Milles wanted to resume using staple ports (ports where incoming foreign 
en|merchants were required to offer their goods for sale before anywhere else) 
en|to force merchants from abroad to use their assets to buy English goods and prevent them from 
en|transferring gold or silver from England homewards. Milles's opinions, however, were not widely valued.
en|One of his contemporaries wrote, "Milles was so much out of step with the time that his pamphlets had little influence."
en|Ferré Aguayo was born in Ponce to a wealthy family. S
en|he was one of six siblings, Jose, Carlos, Hernan, Rosario and Luis, Puerto Rico's former 
en|governor. When she was 21, Ferré traveled to the United States where 
en|she commenced her novitiate. After five years, she completed the solemn vows. 
en|As part of her religious work, Ferré traveled back and forth between Puerto Rico
en|and the United States, serving as an abbess in Cabo Rojo and New York City.
en|During this time frame, she attended various universities in the United States,
en|studying sociology and arts. After working as a member of New York City's Committee 
en|Against Poverty, to which she was appointed by Mayor John Lindsay, 
en|Ferré decided in 1969, to set her permanent residence in Ponce, 
en|specifically in the low-income sector of La Playa.
nl|Wikipedia is een online encyclopedie die ernaar streeft om
nl|in alle erkende talen informatie te bieden die objectief, verifieerbaar en 
nl|vrij herbruikbaar is. Het project is gebaseerd op vijf basisprincipes.
nl|De Nederlandstalige versie startte op 19 juni 2001 
nl|en is met meer dan 2,2 miljoen artikelen de op
nl|vijf na grootste van circa 360 taalversies.
nl|De encyclopedie is vrij bewerkbaar. Dat houdt in dat iedereen tekst 
nl|en afbeeldingen kan toevoegen of aanpassen, met inachtneming van de basisregels.
nl|Voor de bewerkers zijn er diverse hulppagina's beschikbaar. 
nl|Er is ook een snelcursus voor nieuwelingen. 
nl|Zaken uitproberen kan in de zandbak en vragen kunnen gesteld 
nl|worden bij de helpdesk. Voor privacyvragen kunt u hier terecht.
